# Tool checksums — AutoMorpheBuilder
#
# SHA-256 digests of every external artifact the pipeline downloads.
# The verify scripts in `.github/scripts/pipeline/` consult this file
# and fail closed on mismatch.
#
# Format: <hex-sha256>  <relative-artifact-name>  # <human note>
# Comments after `#` are ignored by `sha256sum -c --strict`.
#
# Most entries are version-pinned. When the upstream version changes
# (new `morphe-desktop` release, new `APKEditor` tag, new SDK build
# tools, new Chromium build), update the corresponding SHA below.
#
# How to refresh:
#   1. Trigger a fresh build (the new SHA will be printed to the log
#      even when the manifest entry is a TODO).
#   2. Compare the printed `Verified SHA-256 for <path>` line against
#      the existing entry in this file.
#   3. If the upstream version changed, replace the line and commit.
#
# See `docs/checksums.md` for the full workflow.

# --- morphe-desktop CLI -----------------------------------------------------
# The Java CLI that drives patching. Hash changes every release.
# Source: https://github.com/MorpheApp/morphe-desktop/releases
# Current: v1.15.0  (verified via gh release download + sha256sum)
727e3744aa5c0006474590de6f4041bd55edc59f3d6cb9b596e95f7116384506  morphe-desktop.jar  # v1.15.0

# --- APKEditor ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Used to merge split packages (base.apk + split_config.*.apk → universal).
# Hash changes every release.
# Source: https://github.com/REAndroid/APKEditor/releases
# Current: V1.4.9  (verified via GitHub API digest + curl + sha256sum)
a9cd40df818845456be6d696de6110c89edf4b0a0580cb83438ed6b25a366e67  APKEditor.jar  # V1.4.9

# --- Android build-tools (aapt / aapt2) --------------------------------------
# The cmdline-tools zip + sdkmanager-produced build-tools dir.
# Google's `dl.google.com/android/repository/...` does NOT publish a
# sibling `.sha256` file, so we cannot pin a hash for the SDK zip
# itself. `install_aapt.sh` prints the actual SHA at the end of each
# install with a TODO note; copy that hash here when you want strict
# verification. The build-tools;35.0.0 contents are deterministic per
# SDK release — once pinned they don't drift within a build-tools
# version line.
#
# TODO(pin-aapt2): drop in the sha256 of build-tools;35.0.0 once captured.

# --- Playwright Chromium (chrome-for-testing) --------------------------------
# The Chrome-for-testing CDN does NOT publish a sibling `.sha256` for
# `chrome-linux64.zip`. SHA changes every Playwright/Chromium version.
# `install_playwright.sh` prints the actual SHA at the end of each
# install with a TODO note; copy that hash here when you want strict
# verification.
#
# TODO(pin-chromium): drop in the sha256 of chrome-linux64.zip once captured.

# --- per-repo *.mpp patches archives ----------------------------------------
# Hash changes per (repo, release-tag) pair — too many entries for a
# single manifest. The existing `Implementation-Version` /
# `cli-tag`/`patch-tag` check in `download_morphe_tools.sh` and
# `fetch_morphe_tools.sh` is the primary gate; SHA-256 verification
# is opt-in via a sibling `checksums/<slug>-<tag>-sha256.txt` file
# that the build would consume. See `docs/checksums.md` for the
# upgrade path.